centtothepilefoundationsoftheextra-largebridge.Themodelinitiallyestablishedhazardindicatorsforshieldtunneling,
utilizingtheminimumdistance-maximumentropyprincipletointegratesubjectiveandobjectiveweights.Subsequently,the
setpairanalysis-variablefuzzysettheorywasemployedtodeterminethehazardlevelofshieldtunneling.Further,thedu
al-factorcatastrophetheorywasintroducedtoestablishbridgevulnerabilityindicatorsandascertainthecorrespondingvul
nerabilitylevel.Finally,therisk matrixmethodwasappliedtocoupletheshieldtunnelinghazardandbridgevulnerability
toobtaintheoverallrisklevelofshieldtunnelingadjacenttothebridgepilefoundations.Theresultsindicatethatthehaz
ardlevelofshieldtunnelingforthisprojectisLevelII ,indicatingarelativelylowrisk.Meanwhile,thebridgevulnerability
levelisLevelII ,signifying mildvulnerability.Thecoupledrisklevelofshieldtunnelinghazardandbridgevulnerabilityis
